  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "ShiftCare stays authoritative",
      "items": [
        "Clients, staff, roster, assignments, care records, documents and service billing stay in ShiftCare.",
        "Workers keep native acceptance, clock-in/out and notes. The bookkeeper approves finance through the existing process.",
        "Native Inbox Signals/referrals require feature access and staff review; they are not proven enabled in OCD's production account."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Gated production paths",
      "items": [
        "Dashed connector/journey paths are proposed. REST needs eligible API access, a key and a verified contract for each action.",
        "Bounded polling is the default proposal. No customer ShiftCare webhook subscription has been verified.",
        "The authenticated Codex MCP is a separate supervised session; it is not the website's credential or an unattended job runner."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Data and visibility",
      "items": [
        "REST replies/read-back refresh the OCD projection. Proposed changes stay pending until remote state is verified.",
        "Real participant/worker identity filtering is required. Private notes, home addresses and other participants' data stay restricted.",
        "Journey input comes from a consented worker device or manual ETA; Mapbox returns routes, not worker location."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Exceptions and finance",
      "items": [
        "Unknown write result: reconcile before retry. Unsupported upload, group cancellation or missing availability: native office handling.",
        "The state store owns requests, approvals, job outcomes and OCD message evidence; it does not replace ShiftCare.",
        "Preserve ShiftCare → Excel/export → Xero and the confirmed payroll platform. No second invoice/pay run."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Evidence and scope",
      "items": [
        "Research: docs/OCD_ShiftCare_Integration_and_Automation_Design.md, sections 2–10; redacted MCP capability evidence is alongside it.",
        "Transcript: intake 351–368/855–873/1168; reminders 536–540/644; care and finance 472–486/693–726.",
        "This is a proposed system architecture, not a claim that backend jobs, writes, live portals or ETA are implemented."
      ]
    }
  ]
